{
  "title": "Model StepResult as a Result-like enum; pin recipes deleted_at => deleted_seq",
  "description": "Left over from the 2026-11-07 CHECK constraints work, which added CHECKs for step_outputs (success/error pairing, output_hash NULL for inline), sessions.token_type, recipe_versions.version_source, recipes.deleted_seq, and the shopping_list_history undo pairing. (1) ramekin-core pipeline/step.rs StepResult still carries success: bool + error: Option<String>, and StepOutputStore::save_output takes the same pair; the server maps the pair to a Result when it writes a row (scraping/output_store.rs step_outcome). \
Making StepResult hold a Result-like outcome touches about 60 constructors and 35 readers across ramekin-core, server and cli, and a failed step can still carry output (the executor saves failure output to root-cause runs), so the enum needs an output on both arms. (2) recipes only has CHECK (deleted_seq IS NULL OR deleted_at IS NOT NULL). \
The converse can't be a CHECK while recipes_stamp_delete sets deleted_seq in an AFTER UPDATE trigger, since the UPDATE that sets deleted_at briefly leaves deleted_seq NULL; it would need the soft delete (api/recipes/delete.rs) to take the clock stamp itself.",
  "status": "open",
